{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534575-what-exactly-does-psychic-lobotomy-protect-you-from","id":1534575,"title":"What exactly does Psychic Lobotomy protect you from?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-22T22:44:49-07:00","id":1534575,"title":"What exactly does Psychic Lobotomy protect you from?","content":"It states in Secrets of the Covenants that the scale Psychic Lobotomy states &quot;Any power which would affect, influence, or read his mind suffer the Dragon\u2019s Coil of Zirnitra dots as a penalty to their dice rolls, and he adds those dots in any contested rolls he makes. This includes many applications of Auspex, Majesty, Dominate, or many psychic Merits.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exactly which parts of Auspex does it protect you from? Is it just Auspex 4? Is it anything dealing with emotions and the mind? Would this prevent someone with Auspex from knowing if you've committed &quot;the big D?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27225-granola","name":"Granola","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T15:46:16-07:00","id":1534741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Granola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534575-what-exactly-does-psychic-lobotomy-protect-you-from#post1534575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It states in Secrets of the Covenants that the scale Psychic Lobotomy states &quot;Any power which would affect, influence, or read his mind suffer the Dragon\u2019s Coil of Zirnitra dots as a penalty to their dice rolls, and he adds those dots in any contested rolls he makes. This includes many applications of Auspex, Majesty, Dominate, or many psychic Merits.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exactly which parts of Auspex does it protect you from? Is it just Auspex 4? Is it anything dealing with emotions and the mind? Would this prevent someone with Auspex from knowing if you've committed &quot;the big D?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess not. As far as I remember, auspex 2 is not contested or resisted. And I guess that is more like feeling you, than really reading your mind. So I would rule, that it does nothing for you. For auspex 4, that yes, would receive the bonus. That's said, there's other ways to hide the big D. And if is really a scale that you want, you could talk to your storyteller (or offer, if you are the storyteller) to create a scale that does that with the rules to create scales from the corebook. I could see something like that for coil of ziva, for instance<br /> <br /> TL/DR<br /> I would say<br /> Protects just from auspex 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","user":"ImortalKiller","date":".  Edit: typos and add TL/DR 04-25-2024, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T19:40:50-07:00","id":1534746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Granola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534575-what-exactly-does-psychic-lobotomy-protect-you-from#post1534575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly which parts of Auspex does it protect you from? Is it just Auspex 4? Is it anything dealing with emotions and the mind? Would this prevent someone with Auspex from knowing if you've committed &quot;the big D?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as Auspex goes, it's 2 and 4, both of which are rolled targeted effects that measure mental/emotional/spiritual phenomena, of which diablerie is a part; Uncanny Perception is filling the niche previously represented with Aura Sight and being a supernatural creature has its effects on the psyche, as does eating souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}